WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.190
The new red-band trailer for the Hellboy reboot
does a magnificent job of setting the franchise's

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:10.630
new tone, revealing a fun take on Hellboy
and the cataclysmic danger in his world and

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:12.540
hinting at some deeper Hellboy lore.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.559
Here's a look at some of the small details
you might have missed.

00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:16.559
Long live the king

00:00:16.559 --> 00:00:20.099
The blazing blade that Hellboy wields in the
red band trailer is a little more than just

00:00:20.099 --> 00:00:21.099
a cool effect.

00:00:21.099 --> 00:00:24.039
It's almost certainly meant to be the mythical
blade Excalibur.

00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:26.679
Yeah, the one King Arthur carried around.

00:00:26.679 --> 00:00:31.039
In The Wild Hunt comic book storyline, it
was revealed that not only can Hellboy wield

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:35.390
Excalibur, but he can do so because he is
a descendant of King Arthur and the true,

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:36.710
rightful heir of the British Isles.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:41.871
As far as wild reveals go, this one may be
one of the wildest in Hellboy history, so

00:00:41.871 --> 00:00:45.980
it's pretty exciting to see this moment being
presented on the big screen.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:46.980
The Wild Hunt

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.540
The Osiris Club, a mysterious organization
ripped from the pages of Hellboy comic books,

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:56.110
appears in the new trailer on a hunt for giants,
astride horseback and decked in some very

00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:01.140
Arthurian green and white tabards, led by
a knight wearing the head of a stag.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:05.180
The existence of the Osiris Club in the film
tracks with the appearance of the villain

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.490
Nimue, played by Milla Jovovich.

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:11.439
It seems like a sure bet that the movie will
rely pretty heavily on the comics for plot

00:01:11.439 --> 00:01:15.969
details, meaning this new movie will be a
treat for longtime Hellboy fans.

00:01:15.969 --> 00:01:16.969
Hellboy in Mexico

00:01:16.969 --> 00:01:20.499
In a blink-and-you'll-miss-it moment, eagle-eyed
viewers may have caught a flash of a giant

00:01:20.499 --> 00:01:23.409
bat-like creature standing in a wrestling
ring.

00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:28.520
Not only is this rad, but it hints a fan-favorite
one-shot story, Hellboy in Mexico.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:33.249
That story details Hellboy getting real with
Abe Sapien about one of the strangest and

00:01:33.249 --> 00:01:35.380
most difficult times in his life.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.939
While in Mexico in the 1950s, he got in deep
with a trio of brothers who also happen to

00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:40.990
be luchadors.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:44.999
These luchadors are more than your average
masked wrestlers: they also hunt monsters

00:01:44.999 --> 00:01:47.939
because they received a vision from the Virgin
Mary.

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:52.579
Hellboy joins them on their quest, which entangles
him with ancient Mayan temples and vampire

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.579
luchadors.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:57.329
A sweet epilogue gives readers a glimpse into
what life could have been like had Hellboy

00:01:57.329 --> 00:02:02.049
stopped hunting monsters, donning a mask and
wrestling for the adoration of the crowd.

00:02:02.049 --> 00:02:06.139
While we probably won't see the whole tale
told in Hellboy, even referencing it, among

00:02:06.139 --> 00:02:10.360
other adventures, will help give viewers a
deeper understanding of the scope of Hellboy's

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:13.870
long history of beating up monsters since
World War II.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:16.110
"C'mon, let's get your game face on."

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.110
"Rrrrr.

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:18.110
Yeah, c’mon!

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:19.110
Let's do this!"

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.110
Fear the Baba Yaga

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:24.650
One of the most striking images in the entire
trailer is the appearance of a house, conspicuously

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:28.160
trotting along on a pair of slender, spindly
chicken legs.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:32.480
That, as you may or may not know, is home
to none other than the Baba Yaga, the notorious

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.670
witch of eastern European folklore.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:38.780
In the Hellboy universe, the Baba Yaga is
known to be incredibly powerful.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:42.870
She's a fearsome witch who's mostly known
for dealing in magic that involves spirits

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:43.870
and souls.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:47.420
She has an army of the undead at her beck
and call, which could be pretty interesting

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.090
in the film, if they show up.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:50.220
Punch your soul out

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:55.820
In the new trailer, a woman named Alice appears
to be a field agent in the employ of the BPRD.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:59.800
From most of what's been shown of the movie,
there doesn't seem to be anything too quirky

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:05.220
or special about her, that is, until she punches
someone so hard their spirit flies out of

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:06.220
them.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:10.500
There's a chance this could have something
to do with the flashy, appropriately BPRD-branded

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.980
brass knuckles she sports in the trailer.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:17.000
There's also a chance that this hints at her
comic book roots as a person deeply affected

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.980
by and connected to the fae.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:24.840
In the 1995 Hellboy comic The Corpse, Hellboy
must rescue Alice as a baby after she's kidnapped

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:26.490
by the King of the Faeries.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:30.510
After being saved, one of the faeries reveals
to Hellboy that they were going to raise Alice

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:34.930
as their own child because something has gone
wrong and faeries are no longer able to have

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:35.930
children.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:40.960
In 2008's The Wild Hunt, Hellboy meets Alice
again and remarks at how young she looks even

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:45.230
though decades have passed, indicating that
her time with the fae has somehow altered

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.230
her.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:49.890
Through the effects of Nimue's treachery,
Alice essentially becomes the new Queen of

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:54.100
the Fairies and struggles to provide sanctuary
for the fae as the world literally goes to

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.100
hell.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.440
Movie Alice may not end up having as grand
a role as she does in the comics, but this

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:03.060
simple shot from the trailer at least hints
at a supernatural connection for the character.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.200
Hell on Earth

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:09.150
It's tough to tell if the giant entity summoned
by Nimue is an aspect of the Ogdru Jahad or

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:13.830
not, but it's likely that the pale, skinless-looking
beast is meant to be something similar to

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:16.169
the Ogdru Jahad of the Hellboy comics.

00:04:16.169 --> 00:04:19.280
The Ogdru Jahad are about as bad as bad guys
get.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.150
They represent one thing and one thing only:
The End of Everything.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:26.420
Many of Hellboy's villains have been working
to summon The Ogdru Jahad.

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:31.510
In fact, Hellboy's own summoning was the result
of an Ogdru Jahad ritual gone wrong.

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:36.060
Whatever the massive entity that's annihilating
London in the trailer actually is, it's definitely

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.720
linked to the end times.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:42.560
So much of what is shown in the trailer hints
at bad, bad things for our heroes… including

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:43.820
a first date gone wrong.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:50.440
"This is not gonna work, y'know, because I'm
a Capricorn, and you're f---ing nuts!"

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:54.050
Will this new film have everything that fans
of the character have been craving since the

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:57.580
last film, Hellboy 2: The Golden Army came
out in 2008?

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:02.550
Based on the details in this trailer, chances
seem pretty good so far…

